From: =?UTF-8?q?Lo=C3=AFc=20Vigneron?= <loic.vigneron@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:12:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] staging: media: tegra-video: Timestamp buffers at frame start

Buffers were stamped when their memory write completed, after the
whole frame had been read out and the capture thread had been
scheduled. Stamp them when the frame start syncpoint is reached
instead, so timestamps from two cameras can be compared to measure
and align their frame timing.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/staging/media/tegra-video/tegra210.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/tegra-video/tegra210.c b/drivers/staging/media/tegra-video/tegra210.c
index da99f19..0f09234 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/tegra-video/tegra210.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/tegra-video/tegra210.c
@@ -377,7 +377,9 @@ static void release_buffer(struct tegra_vi_channel *chan,
 
 	vb->sequence = chan->sequence++;
 	vb->field = V4L2_FIELD_NONE;
-	vb->vb2_buf.timestamp = ktime_get_ns();
+	/* A captured buffer carries the time of its frame start. */
+	if (state != VB2_BUF_STATE_DONE)
+		vb->vb2_buf.timestamp = ktime_get_ns();
 	vb2_buffer_done(&vb->vb2_buf, state);
 }
 
@@ -486,6 +488,8 @@ static int tegra_channel_capture_frame(struct tegra_vi_channel *chan,
 		}
 	}
 
+	buf->buf.vb2_buf.timestamp = ktime_get_ns();
+
 	if (capture_timedout) {
 		dev_err_ratelimited(&chan->video.dev,
 				    "frame start syncpt timeout: %d\n", err);
